D. COMPLETING/EDITING THE FORM
1. Form Completion Checklist
Immediately following the interview, the interviewer will review the form for completeness
using the CARDIA Diet History Form Completion Checklist (Appendix 5). This checklist is
designed as a reminder of all of the information needed to satisfactorily complete the Dietary
Practices and Quantitated Food Frequency forms. It should be reviewed prior to and following
the interview to insure that all information necessary to process the form has been obtained and
is recorded. It should also be used as a basis for questioning during the interview and when
checking forms completed by other nutritionists.
Post-interview responsibilities include making certain the following are present on the form:
1. the participant’s bar code identification;
2. beginning and ending time for interview;
3. an answer for each question in the Dietary Practices section;
4. a check mark in either the space next to “NO” or the space next to “YES” for each food
group or subgroup in the Quantitated Food Frequency;
5. serving size and amount for each food item reported by participant entered and circled;
6. “legal” serving units determined and recorded for each food item reported by
participant which was not listed on Quantitated Food Frequency;
7. frequencies for each food item reported by participant;
8. frequencies for additions dependent on the food items to which they are added;
9. applicable prep codes for each food item reported by participant;
10. a fat code for each food item with a prep code reported by participant;
11. Food IDs for food items identified by brand name;
12. Food IDs for food items labeled with an asterisk (*);
13. serving size and amount circled for all foods recorded
