Date and Time Variables

All dates and times are stored as SAS date and time variables.
SAS stores all dates as the number of days since January 1, 1960,
and all times as the number of seconds since 12:00:00 AM. To ease
use of these variables, they have been saved with the SAS formats
DATE7. and TIMES5.. Due to time constraints, the only time
variables edited were collections times; edits were not done to any
return times or processing times for this version.

Number of Aliquots Collected

While most participants had a maximum of three aliquots
collected from each collection period, some participants had four
aliquots collected. The fourth aliquot was collected for quality
control procedures.

Computed Variables
Three types of variables are calculated in this dataset:
(1) C39LENG1, C39LENG2, C39LENG3
The length of each collection period was calculated with
the following algorithm (Collection 1 used as an
example). Calculations assume an approximate 24 hour
period.

C39LENG1 = .;
DIFF1 = C39EDAT1 - C39UDAT1;
IF DIFF1=0 THEN DO;
C39LENG1=(C39ETIM1-C39BTIM1) /3600;
END;
IF DIFF1=1 THEN DO;
C39LENG1=( (C39ETIM1+86400) -C39BTIM1) /3600;
END;
IF DIFF1=2 THEN DO;
C39LENG1=( (C39ETIM1+172800) -C39BTIM1) /3600;
END;

